    "result_text": "Done. The structured address form is implemented and the full test suite is green (2/2 passing, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\n**Contract (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)** \u2014 added `addressLine1` and optional `addressLine2` to the `OwnerFields` schema (so they flow into both the request DTO and the `Owner` response DTO, which is generated at build time), and removed `address` from the `required` list so a structured-only request is still contract-valid. Backward-compatible: the flat `address` remains accepted.\n\n**Composition & normalization (`NormalizeOwnerAddress.java`)** \u2014 the POST pipeline's first step now prefers the structured form when `addressLine1` is non-blank: it normalizes each supplied line (trim/collapse-whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET` etc.) and sets the flat `address` to the composed value \u2014 normalized `addressLine1`, plus a single space and normalized `addressLine2` when `addressLine2` is present. When no `addressLine1` is given, it normalizes the flat `address` as before.\n\n**Validity (either-form)** \u2014 because the normalize step writes the effective address into `request.address` before `RequireOwnerFields` runs, the existing required-field check already enforces \"an address in either form (non-blank `addressLine1` or flat `address`) plus city\" with no change: a request with neither leaves a blank composed address and is rejected. Everything downstream (household hash, postcode validation, locality \u2014 all keyed off city/postcode plus the now-normalized stored address) reads the effective values.\n\n**Persistence** \u2014 added `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` fields (with getters/setters) to the `Owner` entity and `address_line1`/`address_line2` columns to all four DB schemas (`hsqldb` \u2014 the one tests use \u2014 plus `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`), so `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns the persisted normalized `addressLine1`. MapStruct auto-maps the new fields by name. I also updated `ApplyOwner` (the PUT path) to copy the structured fields for consistency.\n\nThe two acceptance tests \u2014 `coreNormalizesAndComposesStructuredAddress` (asserts `addressLine1` \u2192 `\"10 KING STREET\"` and composed `address` \u2192 `\"10 KING STREET\"`) and `functionalityStillAcceptsFlatAddress` \u2014 both pass.",
